{
  "name": "PassedOnUnread",
  "comment": "A format type keeps its raw bytes until first use (ruling 6): a json file read and\nwritten back on, unchanged, is byte-for-byte the same. config.json is spelled with\nunusual whitespace and keys out of order so any re-parse-and-write would reformat and\nthe hashes would diverge. The copy is deleted at the end. If this is green today (today's\nfile passthrough already preserves bytes), mark it a guard — stage 3 must keep it green.",
  "step": [
